@packages/core/src/model.sigil import { SigilSemanticModel }

component SigilDiagnostics {
  goal {
    Construct stable machine-readable diagnostics for recoverable Sigil source,
    configuration, workspace, resolution, and optional host-enrichment problems.

    Keep core-stage diagnostic creation independent from required host failures and
    higher core stages while allowing hosts to diagnose recoverable optional
    enrichment failures.
  }

  interface {
    DiagnosticConstruction {
      diagnostic(code, message, options?) returns a SigilDiagnostic

      severity defaults to error when omitted

      options may provide severity, file path, and source range
    }

    DiagnosticCode {
      diagnostic codes are stable identifiers that consumers may interpret without
      parsing messages
    }
  }
}

expand SigilDiagnostics {
  constraints {
    DiagnosticConstruction {
      Diagnostic construction depends only on SigilSemanticModel data.

      Parsing, configuration, workspace, and resolution problems use diagnostics when
      partial results remain meaningful.

      Required core filesystem and runtime failures are not converted into Sigil
      diagnostics.

      Hosts may convert an optional enrichment failure into a diagnostic when the
      primary result remains meaningful.
    }

    DiagnosticCode {
      Every diagnostic code has one stable severity-bearing machine-readable
      representation.

      SIGIL_UNUSED_IMPORT is an error for one resolved imported name without
      qualifying local use.

      SIGIL_EXPAND_WITHOUT_COMPONENT is an error when an expand is neither colocated
      with its component nor connected to it through a resolved named import.

      SIGIL_DETACHED_LITERAL_BLOCK is an error when a blank line separates
      introducing prose from an opening fence.

      SIGIL_LITERAL_WITHOUT_INTRODUCTION is an error when an opening fence has no
      preceding prose in its section or concept block.

      SIGIL_UNCLOSED_LITERAL_BLOCK is an error when no qualifying closing fence
      occurs.

      SIGIL_INVALID_LITERAL_TYPE is an error when a literal type does not match
      [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_+.-]*.

      SIGIL_LINE_TOO_LONG is informational when ordinary prose can be canonically
      wrapped to the 79-character content width.

      SIGIL_UNFORMATTABLE_LINE is an error when one indivisible prose token exceeds
      the 79-character content width.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    DiagnosticConstruction {
      Decision: Permit hosts to convert a host failure into a structured diagnostic
      only when it occurs during optional enrichment and a meaningful primary result
      remains available.

      Scope: Governs diagnostic construction by core consumers after successful
      primary processing; required core filesystem, runtime, workspace-loading, and
      resolution failures continue to propagate.

      Trade-offs: Callers retain useful partial results but must inspect diagnostics
      to determine whether optional enrichment is incomplete.

      Discarded alternatives: Converting every host failure hides required-operation
      failure boundaries, while propagating optional enrichment failures discards
      meaningful primary results.

      Consequences: Hosts may report optional enrichment incompleteness without
      changing required core failure semantics.
    }
  }

  cases {
    DiagnosticCode {
      An unknown section produces a source-ranged SIGIL_UNKNOWN_SECTION diagnostic.

      An unsupported configured language version produces SIGIL_UNSUPPORTED_VERSION.

      An imports-only _module.sigil produces SIGIL_MODULE_WITHOUT_COMPONENT.

      A contiguous ungrouped interface region produces warning
      SIGIL_MISSING_CONCEPT_IDENTIFIER.

      An identifier outside [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]* produces error
      SIGIL_INVALID_CONCEPT_IDENTIFIER.

      An empty concept block produces error SIGIL_EMPTY_CONCEPT_BLOCK.

      A nested concept block produces error SIGIL_NESTED_CONCEPT_BLOCK.

      Two different accessible concepts with identifiers equal without regard to case
      produce error SIGIL_AMBIGUOUS_CONCEPT_IDENTIFIER.

      A valid identifier that is not PascalCase or contains a hyphen or underscore
      produces informational SIGIL_CONCEPT_IDENTIFIER_STYLE.

      An optional ownership-source enumeration failure produces warning
      SIGIL_IMPLEMENTATION_SOURCE_DISCOVERY when primary context data remains
      available.

      One unused name in a multi-name resolved import produces one
      SIGIL_UNUSED_IMPORT at that imported name.

      An unimported cross-file expand produces SIGIL_EXPAND_WITHOUT_COMPONENT at the
      expand declaration.

      Apparent imports, components, concepts, or braces inside a LiteralBlock produce
      no structural or reference diagnostic.

      Leading indentation does not contribute to SIGIL_LINE_TOO_LONG or
      SIGIL_UNFORMATTABLE_LINE.
    }

    DiagnosticConstruction {
      Omitting severity constructs an error diagnostic.

      A filesystem permission failure during a required operation rejects the host
      operation instead of producing a Sigil diagnostic.

      A filesystem permission failure during optional host enrichment can produce a
      diagnostic while preserving the primary result.
    }
  }
}
